From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v0lumehi <aljic.zijad@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:21:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Controllers: a radial deadzone for each stick
 (DM_STICK_DEADZONE_L / _R)

A physical controller's sticks reach the guest as the controller reports them. A worn or drifting stick
cannot be corrected without a front end of its own. DM_STICK_DEADZONE_L and DM_STICK_DEADZONE_R take a whole
percent of the travel (1..50). Inside it the stick reads centred, outside it the remaining travel is
rescaled so a stick pushed all the way still reads full. Unset, 0 or any other value leaves the stick as
reported. The deadzone sits in dm_pad_set_player, which every physical controller passes through on the Mac
and the iPhone. Keyboard, touch and scripted input do not use it.

stick_deadzone.h holds the pure math (the same radial rescale steam_deadzone uses) and
t_stick_deadzone.c tests the switch text, the unchanged default, the centred inside, the rescale, full travel
and monotonic output. docs/env_switches.tsv lists both switches.

Upstream-Status: pending [seedds/nxnative#TBD, becomes forwarded when the PR is open]
Reason: The Mac launcher's Controls settings offer left and right deadzones with a live preview and need a general engine switch
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1025
